## Workflow Rules

### Planning & artifacts
- UI plans and SPECs live under **`.work.ui/`** only — not `.work/features/` for screens.
- Domain/API behaviour: link `.work/features/` SPECs — do not duplicate API contracts in screen SPECs.
- Wait for approval before large UI refactors when the user asked for plan/spec only.

### Deletion
- NEVER delete files without explicit user permission.

### Git
- NEVER `git commit` / `git push` unless the user explicitly requests it in the same message.
- Session commits: use `@session-control close commit` (Agent OS) when adopted.

### No Attribution
- No "Generated by", "Created by AI", or agent signatures in source or SPEC files.

---

## Verification & Quality (UI)

### UI task gate (per task)
1. Read screen SPEC before editing.
2. Run lint, typecheck, unit tests for touched packages.
3. Scope check: only declared files in `NEXT_UI.md` task row.
4. UIS-06 when agent-assisted; UIS-07 when craft tier ≥ refined; UIS-08 for all screens; UIS-09 for analytical dashboards.

### Before milestone complete
- `@ui-visual-verify milestone`
- `@ui-accessibility-audit milestone`

### On failure
- Paste exact errors; fix; re-run gate. Do not mark task `done` on failure.

